<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">El Jadida</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mazagan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">El Jadida, formerly Mazagan, is a port city on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a>. The Portuguese fortified it from 1514 and made it their last stronghold in Morocco, holding it until 1769, when they evacuated it under siege. The Portuguese City of Mazagan, with its star-shaped ramparts and great cistern, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/el-jadida.jpg" alt="El Jadida" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.Rais · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forteresse_Jadida_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
